l for long-distance flights, and his concern for others may mitigate cooperation issues. B's technical strengths are good but his interpersonal issues may be more problematic. So we might shift to A.\n\nBut we also need to bring up C and D later. For now, we can argue that A is a stronger alternative and perhaps should be the leading candidate. So we can change our vote to Candidate A, providing reasoning.\n\nWe need to reference prior discussion: Agent 2 recommended B, but we are less convinced because of crew cooperation concerns and A's strengths.\n\nThus, public message: state vote for Candidate A, explain why.\n\nLet's produce."}
